#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""V46 — Learned Overlapping Slow Pathways.

Locked question
---------------
Can experience learn *where* durable sharing should occur so a bounded,
slot-free slow memory preserves PAIR's useful transfer while reducing V45's
cross-identity / different-outcome interference?

V46 changes one operation only: allocation of the same 1,024 slow units among
several overlapping learning pathways.  There are no permanent slots, no
replay, no corroboration gate, no factor-coded output, and no larger state.

Mac M3 quick start
------------------
  python3 elm_v46_learned_pathways.py --self-test
  caffeinate -dimsu python3 elm_v46_learned_pathways.py --stage primary \\
      --workers 4 --out-dir v46_results
  caffeinate -dimsu python3 elm_v46_learned_pathways.py --stage full \\
      --workers 4 --out-dir v46_results

Rerunning the same command reuses verified completed jobs and resumes partial
jobs from atomic checkpoints.
"""
